.TH "TRCC\-DEVICE" "1" "" "trcc\-linux 9.8.5" "TRCC Manual"
.SH NAME
trcc\-device \- Discover and connect to TRCC devices
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtrcc device\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Discover and connect to TRCC devices.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS connect
.PP
\fBtrcc device connect\fR \fIKEY\fR
.PP
Open USB transport and perform the wire\-protocol handshake.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS disconnect
.PP
\fBtrcc device disconnect\fR \fIKEY\fR
.PP
Close the transport and drop the device.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
(no description)
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS list
.PP
\fBtrcc device list\fR
.PP
List devices currently attached to the host.
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS reset
.PP
\fBtrcc device reset\fR \fIKEY\fR
.PP
Disconnect + clear cached state for a device. Use this when the LCD seems stuck  \-  drops any cached frame, theme, and runtime counters. Re\-running connect after this starts completely fresh.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
(no description)
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS select
.PP
\fBtrcc device select\fR \fIORDINAL\fR
.PP
Persist the active\-device selection by ordinal. Multi\-device hosts (e.g. two LCDs + one LED controller) need a way to point CLI commands at "the one I'm steering today". Resolves the ordinal against device list and stores the resulting key in AppSettings.active_device.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBORDINAL\fR
1\-based ordinal of the attached device to mark active (matches device list output)
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBtrcc\fR(1)
